{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "HTML Attributes"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "A1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when talking about HTML attributes."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe common simple incidents at work in a simple spoken or written situation with a supportive interlocutor. Assess the incident of data in the macrosystem processes, based on the data dictionary to consolidate intervening data, based in established parameters."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.  Exchanges simple information on programming tools and solutions to a client's requirement."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Indefinite Pronouns in Affirmative Statements"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use <span class=\"strong\"> indefinite pronouns</span> when we want to refer to an unspecified person, thing or amount."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\"> Indefinite pronouns</span> are used to talk about things or people without mentioning exactly what or who they are. </br></br>  Examples: </br>  <i><span class=\"strong\"> Everybody</span> uses HTML to create programs. </i></br> <i><span class=\"strong\"> Someone</span> is teaching me how to use HTML attributes. </i></br>  When using an <span class=\"strong\">indefinite pronoun</span> you have to conjugate the verb in singular. </br></br>  Example: </br>  <i><span class=\"strong\">Everyone</span> works with the browser. </i></br>  However, if you need to make reference to the <span class=\"strong\">indefinite pronoun again</span>, the subject pronoun that you use goes generally in <i>plural</i>. </br></br>  Example: </br>  <i><span class=\"strong\">Everybody</span> in the company knows about HTML attributes. They receive constant training. </i>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">People</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Things</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Places</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Somebody - Someone\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Something\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Somewhere\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Everybody - Everyone\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Everything\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Everywhere\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "That's why everyone is familiar with terms like HTML."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I dare to say that everybody knows how to use HTML attributes."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Would you like to add something else?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Everyone can learn how to manage HTML attributes, but you have to be careful because somebody can get confused if you use the wrong attribute."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Generic Attributes"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "There are many HTML's attributes that are easy to use with many of the HTML tags. Those attributes are called <span class=\"strong\">generic attributes</span>."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Attribute</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Function</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Options</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Align \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Horizontal alignign\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Right, left, center\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Valign\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Vertical align\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Top, middle, bottom\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"background\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"places a background behind an element\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"URL\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"id\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Names an element, it is used with CSS\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"User defined\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Class\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Classifies an element, it us used with CSS \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"User defined\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Title\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Pop-up titles\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"User defined\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "wrong"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not correct or mistaken"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Everyone can learn how to manage HTML attributes, but you have to be careful because somebody can get confused if you use the wrong attribute."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob05aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "align"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to put in a straight line"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: < p > is the tag for paragraph and it is part of the align attribute."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob05aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "class attribute"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in HTML is the tool used to associate an element with a style sheet"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are three types of attributes: Core attributes in which we can find id, title, class attribute, and style."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob05aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "dir attribute "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in HTML this tool indicates the direction in which the text flows"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Maybe you can list some types of attributes."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob05aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look on internet and create a definition for HTML attributes."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Mention the characteristics of an attribute, give examples."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Mention the types of attributes a websites can have."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Present your poster to your classmates"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I can define and describe HTML attributes."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I can demonstrate the properties of attributes and give examples."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I can list the types of attributes for HTML."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I can produce a poster about HTML attributes and present it to my classmates."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "list"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "series of names printed in sequence"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Maybe you can list some types of attributes."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob05aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "id": 0, "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome"}, {"_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "template_override": 1, "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n2le02ob05re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n2le02ob05re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Teacher:</span>Good afternoon, class! It is time for your oral exam. Beth, please stand up and answer the questions I'm going to ask you.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\"> Beth: </span> Good afternoon, Teacher. Ok, I'm ready!<br />\n<span class=\"strong\"> Teacher: </span>Nowadays, globalization and new technologies are allowing people to know more about computer programming programs and its components. That's why everyone is familiar with terms like HTML. As we all now, HTML has attributes which contain extra bits of information. I dare to say that everybody knows how to use HTML attributes. But, tell me, Beth, what do we use these attributes for? <br />"}, {"time": "36500", "image": "enpe8n2le02ob05re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Beth: </span> Attributes determine the properties of an HTML element.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Teacher: </span>That's correct, Beth. You find these attributes inside the opening tag. Everyone can learn how to manage HTML attributes, but you have to be careful since somebody, a programmer or any person who needs to use a computer programming program, can get confused if you use the wrong attribute. Now, tell me, how many parts do these attributes have? <br />"}, {"time": "62000", "image": "enpe8n2le02ob05re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Beth: </span>They have two parts: One is the name, which is the property you want to set on the page, and the other one is the value. For example, < p > is the tag for paragraph and it is part of the align attribute, and left, center or right are the values for that paragraph.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Teacher: </span>Good answer, Beth! Is there anything else you can say? Maybe you can list some types of attributes.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Beth: </span>Sure. There are three types of attributes: Core attributes in which we can find id, title, class attribute, and style; internalization attributes which are dir, lang, and xml:lang; as well as the generic attributes.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Teacher: </span>Would you like to add something else?<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Beth: </span>No. I think that's all.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Teacher: </span>Thank you and good job, Beth!\"<br />"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n2le02ob05re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can say what an attribute for an HTML tag is. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about the elements that compose an attribute for an HTML tag. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can list the different types of attributes for HTML tags."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Why do you think HTML is considered a text language?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What image formats do you work with?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "te